<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Achterhoek</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Achterhoek ('back corner') is a rural region in the east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gelderland">Gelderland</a>, bordering <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. Historically part of the County of Zutphen, it is a land of farms, woods and small towns such as Doetinchem, Winterswijk and Groenlo, and its fortified towns were fought over during the Eighty Years' War.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/achterhoek.jpg" alt="Achterhoek" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:Arch · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:LocatieAchterhoekprovinciaal-algemeen.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
